; Under a floor. No `(vertex …)` against `:min 1`.
;
; You cannot know a head is absent until the children run out, so this one
; has no child to point at and lands on the form's own head, the same
; place a missing required key lands.
;
;   positional_missing at [render-pipeline]
;   form `render-pipeline` requires at least 1 `vertex` positional child, found 0
;
; The `(constant …)` below helps not at all: a child counts towards a head
; only if its own head matches byte-for-byte, so nothing can stand in for a
; missing `vertex`. Nor would an out-of-set head; that one fails
; `not_head_member` and still satisfies nobody's floor.
;
;   sjon validate examples/plugins/head-counts/{plugin,example-missing}.sjon

(render-pipeline :name no-vertex
  (fragment :entry fs_main)
  (constant :name gamma :value 2.2))
